   "text": {
    "L1": "India has national symbols that help us understand our country.",
    "L2": "The flag has saffron, white and green bands, with a navy-blue Ashoka Chakra in the middle.",
    "L3": "Saffron stands for courage and strength, white for peace and truth, and green for growth and fertile land.",
    "L4": "The Ashoka Chakra has 24 spokes. It stands for the wheel of law and moving forward.",
    "L5": "The national emblem comes from the Lion Capital of Ashoka at Sarnath. Four lions sit back to back, and below them are the words Satyameva Jayate: Truth alone triumphs.",
    "L6": "India became free on 15 August 1947. On 26 January 1950, the Constitution came into force and India became a republic.",
    "L7": "In a republic, people choose their leaders by voting. A king or queen does not rule just because they were born into the job.",
    "L8": "Remember three symbols: the tiger is our national animal, the peacock our national bird, and the lotus our national flower."
   },
